  "name": "Web Agents Should Adopt the Plan-Then-Execute Paradigm",
  "notes": "The annotation and scope were reviewed against the complete retained original arXiv abstract. Experiments, reported performance and artifact availability have not been independently reproduced. Directly analyzes browser-agent prompt-injection boundaries and WebArena task structure, but advocates typed website operations rather than demonstrating a new GUI-control policy.",
  "published_at": "2026-05-14",
  "relations": [],
  "review_status": "curated",
  "scope": "adjacent",
  "summary": "Argues for compiling web tasks into predefined execution graphs before exposing an agent to untrusted runtime content. Its WebArena task analysis identifies typed, semantically complete website tools as a prerequisite and distinguishes this interface proposal from reactive click-level control.",
